data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002 — greet, tested\\n\\n## What I created\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `src/__init__.py` — empty, added so `tests/test_greet.py` can\\n  `from src.greet import greet` when run from the repo root. This is the\\n  one file outside the two explicitly named in the dispatch; it exists\\n  solely to make `src` importable as a package for test discovery.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` — unit tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: asserts `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: asserts `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n## Test run\\n\\nCommand (run from repo root `~/subject`):\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n    OK\\n\\nExit code: 0 (confirmed via `echo $?` immediately after the run).\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit\\n`4bda13b`: \\\"Add greet function with unit tests\\\". Working tree is clean\\notherwise (only untracked `__pycache__` dirs from the test run, not\\ncommitted).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nNo files outside `src/greet.py`, `src/__init__.py`, and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` were touched.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

